{0 sqlml}

Write [.sql] files with sqlc-style annotations; sqlml asks PostgreSQL for the
parameter and result types of each query and emits typed OCaml.

{1 Packages}

- [sqlml] — the runtime that generated code depends on. See {!module:Sqlml}.
- [sqlml-postgresql] — the [sqlml] command and a libpq driver, [Sqlml_pg].
- [sqlml-caqti] — a Caqti/Eio driver with pooling, [Sqlml_caqti].

{1 Entry points}

- {!module:Sqlml} — [fetch_one], [fetch_all], [exec], [transaction].
- {!module:Sqlml.Row} — decoders used by generated code.
- {!module:Sqlml.Value} — encoders used by generated code.
- {!module:Sqlml.Query} — the shape of a generated query module.
